  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ukraine: Supporting International Dialogue on Accountability for Ukraine: Secretariat Dialogue Group</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1) To establish the Secretariat of the Dialogue Group on Accountability for Ukraine and provide needs-based technical support to the Dialogue Group Workstreams and their respective co-chairs. 2) To maintain secure and reliable rules, techniques, and environment for the Workstream related data storage and exchange. 3) To support the Dialogue Group Secretariat with facilitation of a more active and practical participation of the Office of the Prosecutor General mid-level management in the Workstreams. 4) To enhance visibility and public awareness of the Dialogue Group&#x2019;s work.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Direct beneficiaries: The Office of the Prosecutor General, the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of Ukraine, the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the Kingdom of the Netherlands, the International Criminal Court, the European Commission, the European Union Agency for Criminal Justice Cooperation, the Dialogue Group on Accountability for Ukraine and its members.Indirect beneficiaries: Wider population of Ukraine.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aimed to advance international dialogue on accountability in Ukraine.</narrative>
  </description>
